Explanation of the two changes:

1. In `driver.gotoURL()`, we now `return` the promise from `Page.navigate(...)`.  That ensures we don’t begin our “wait for onload” timers until Chrome has actually accepted the navigate command—this closes a small race window where the page might fire its load event before our monitoring has been set up.

2. In `GatherRunner.pass()`, we wrap the call to `loadPage(...)` in a `Promise.race(...)` against the same 45 s fallback timer (`Driver.MAX_WAIT_FOR_FULLY_LOADED`).  If the page never signals its `loadEventFired`, we still resolve and move on after 45 s, rather than hanging indefinitely.
